WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:22.444
Hi there! Who are you?

2
00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:26.133
I'm a walrus.

3
00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:31.832
Walruses are big sea mammals.

4
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:34.686
Where do you live?

5
00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:41.475
We live near the Arctic Circle.

6
00:00:41.476 --> 00:00:46.113
It is very cold here!

7
00:00:46.114 --> 00:00:49.515
How do you stay warm?

8
00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:53.556
We have lots of blubber.

9
00:00:53.557 --> 00:00:57.580
Blubber is a type of fat.

10
00:00:57.581 --> 00:01:02.881
It keeps us nice and warm.

11
00:01:02.882 --> 00:01:07.610
You have huge tusks!

12
00:01:07.611 --> 00:01:12.925
Our tusks are long teeth.

13
00:01:12.926 --> 00:01:18.257
We use them to poke holes in ice.

14
00:01:18.258 --> 00:01:22.939
Our tusks also protect us from enemies.

15
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.666
Can you swim?

16
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:30.397
Walruses swim very well.

17
00:01:30.398 --> 00:01:34.116
We're not fast.

18
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:40.554
But we can swim for a long time.

19
00:01:40.555 --> 00:01:43.219
What do you eat?

20
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:49.462
Walruses mostly eat clams from the ocean floor.

21
00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:59.133
We use our whiskers to find the clams.

22
00:01:59.134 --> 00:02:02.964
Do you live with other walruses?

23
00:02:02.965 --> 00:02:08.742
Yes, walruses live in big groups.

24
00:02:08.743 --> 00:02:16.509
We like to lie on the beach together.

25
00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:20.036
It's time to sleep now.

26
00:02:20.037 --> 00:02:23.109
Good-bye!

27
00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:34.869
Good-bye, Walrus!
